57
00:03:41,090 --> 00:03:43,650
So I'll talk about
quickly what Expo is.

58
00:03:43,650 --> 00:03:50,050
Expo is a framework that
is built on React Native.

59
00:03:50,050 --> 00:03:53,470
And React Native is a framework
that adapted React.js.

60
00:03:53,470 --> 00:03:58,220
React.js was made
by Meta, which would

61
00:03:58,220 --> 00:04:01,220
use-- at the time was
Facebook, for creating

62
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:04,920
their dynamic, data-driven
social media app.

63
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:08,280
And that's what Expo and
React and React Native,

64
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:12,540
et cetera, is data-driven apps.

65
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:17,660
It allows you to build reusable
UI elements that render

66
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:20,100
differently, depending
on whatever data

67
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:23,020
you have available to
your app or for that user

68
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:26,940
or for that scenario.

69
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:32,380
And we'll go ahead
and show how to make

70
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:34,660
reusable portions
of your app and how

71
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:37,965
to make those data
dependent, data driven.

72
00:04:37,965 --> 00:04:39,340
One of the best
things about Expo

73
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:43,220
is you can build
for web, mobile,

74
00:04:43,220 --> 00:04:47,460
Android and iOS, both mobile
platforms, all with one code

75
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:47,960
base.

76
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,100
So you reduce the amount
of work that you're

77
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:55,820
doing to create an app to hit
as many users as possible,

78
00:04:55,820 --> 00:05:00,020
or make your app available
to as many users as possible.

