there might be a couple of SDKs
that are slightly different,

247
00:15:23,490 --> 00:15:24,740
but it'll show you which ones.

248
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:26,790
But the main difference
is going to be setting up

249
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:29,430
your environment variables.

250
00:15:29,430 --> 00:15:34,590
On Mac OS, you're going to
update your zprofile or Z shell

251
00:15:34,590 --> 00:15:38,410
RC it says, or bash.

252
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:40,050
If you don't know if
you're using bash,

253
00:15:40,050 --> 00:15:42,450
you're probably using
Z shell on Mac OS.

254
00:15:42,450 --> 00:15:46,800
Z shell is the default. And
you'll just add this text

255
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:50,040
to your Z shell RC.

256
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:52,100
On Windows, it's a little
bit more complicated.

257
00:15:52,100 --> 00:15:56,920
But again, it will
step you through that.

258
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,960
I've got it running here.

259
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:07,080
So once you've got it running,
you can click this here.

260
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:11,200
I don't know why that's popping
up on this other screen.

261
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:15,820
OK, so you can see this
image here on their website.

262
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:19,440
It pops you up in
SDK manager, which

